<title>CANADA: Canadian chicken output quotas set for Jan-March.</title>
<headline>Canadian chicken output quotas set for Jan-March.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quotas were set for chicken production in Canada's supply managed industry for Jan 19 and March 15 period, Ontario Chicken Producers said.</p>
<p>Canada will implement a new planned chicken export policy as of March 16, the Canadian Chicken Marketing Agency said.</p>
<p>PROVINCE	     QUOTA (kg eviscerated)</p>
<p>British Columbia   16,100,000</p>
<p>Alberta		10,009,802</p>
<p>Saskatchewan	  2,378,160</p>
<p>Manitoba		4,206,600</p>
<p>Ontario		37,726,813</p>
<p>Quebec		 33,121,900</p>
<p>New Brunswick	 3,253,686</p>
<p>Nova Scotia	   3,698,468</p>
<p>Prince Edward Island  426,000 Newfoundland	  1,877,337</p>
<p>CANADA:	     112,798,766</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548))</p>
